# {% .ProjectName%} Constitution

## Core Principles

### I. Configuration-Driven Generation
A single validated `project.config.yaml` is the source of truth. The generator must never produce unused dependencies or modules.

### II. Standalone Generated Projects
Every generated project must work independently of the generator.

### III. AI-First Development
Provide a root `AGENTS.md` and scoped instructions. Agents must not silently change architecture or suppress failing tests.

### IV. Type Safety and Quality
TypeScript strict mode; Python type annotations, Ruff, Pyright, pytest.

### V. Free and Open-Source First
Prefer free, open-source components.

### VI. Security by Default
Never commit secrets. Use least-privilege OAuth scopes. Run containers as non-root.

### VII. Incremental Implementation
Use specifications, plans, and tasks for substantial changes.

### VIII. Reproducibility and Maintainability
Pin dependencies through supported lockfiles.

## Governance

This constitution supersedes all other practices. Amendments require a written proposal, approval, and a migration plan.
